    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0502" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857M31</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-29T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2860. Department advised that liner <hi rendition="#italic">Manchester
                        Engineer</hi> was torpedoed without warning off Waterford, March 27, with
                    American citizens on board. Please inquire of the Foreign Minister as to whether
                    vessel was sunk by submarine belonging to Germany or her allies. A prompt answer
                    is expected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
